{{Quote|Captain Syndulla I presume, I am Erskin Semaj, senatorial attaché.|Erskin Semaj, to Hera Syndulla|<ref name="Secret Cargo" />}}
'''Erskin Semaj''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[commander]] who served as an [[aide]] to [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] in the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Galactic Senate]] and in her [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|rebellious affairs]], secretly as an agent of [[Luthen Rael]]'s [[Axis network]]. He was instrumental in Mothma's escape from [[Coruscant]] alongside [[Captain]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] immediately following her public denouncement of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]]. He and members of [[Gold Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Gold Squadron]] worked alongside [[Hera Syndulla]]'s [[Spectres]]' rebel cell, [[Phoenix Squadron]], during the [[Operation Handoff|mission]] to escort Mon Mothma to [[Dantooine]] to rally a united rebel fleet. Erskin continued to serve loyally under Mothma in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. 

==Biography==
===Senatorial aide===
Erskin Semaj was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] born on the [[planet]] [[Naboo]] to a [[Chandrilan]] [[Erskin Semaj's father|father]] and a [[Ghorman (people)|Ghorman]] [[Erskin Semaj's mother|mother]]. Semaj's mother was a woman whom his father was having an affair with. Eventually, when his mother died, Semaj was taken in by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]], becoming her [[aide]].<ref name="DB" />

Semaj served as [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]]'s senatorial attaché in [[4 BBY]]. That [[Standard year|year]], he attended the [[Wedding of Stekan Sculdun and Leida Mothma]] on Mothma's homeworld of [[Chandrila]] where he helped her welcome the guests and reported on a parking issue with the [[governor]]'s new [[speeder]].<ref name="One Year Later">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref> Two [[Standard day|days]] later, during the post-wedding party, he spoke with the secret rebel leader [[Luthen Rael]] about his family life. Rael, a collaborator with Mothma in the [[Axis network|burgeoning rebellion]],<ref name="Harvest">{{Andor|Harvest}}</ref> recruited Semaj to work secretly for him while he continued to serve Mothma. Continuing to dutifully serve the Senator, Semaj protected Mothma in ways she was not aware of.<ref name="Welcome" />

[[File:Erskin_and_mon.png|thumb|left|240px|Erskin Semaj accompanies Mon Mothma during a vote run]]
During the [[Senate Investiture|Senate Investiture Week]] in [[3 BBY]], Semaj accompanied Mothma during her attempt to collect votes from her fellow Senators in an attempt to repeal the [[Public Order Resentencing Directive]]. Semaj walked with Mothma as she unsuccessfully attempted to persuade a [[Tarsunt]] senator, while himself speaking to an [[Ottegan]].<ref name="Been to Ghorman?">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}}</ref> The next day, during the recitation of the [[Oathkeeper|Imperial Oath]] in the Senate, Semaj accompanied Mothma as she stormed out of the [[Convocation Chambers]].<ref name="Evening">{{Andor|What a Festive Evening}}</ref>

===Axis allies===
In [[2 BBY]], the Empire began [[Ghorman Massacre|slaughtering]] the Ghorman people, claiming to be putting down an insurrection.<ref name="Who Are You?">{{Andor|Who Are You?}}</ref> That night, while Senator Mon Mothma prepared a speech to condemn the killings, Semaj located a listening device hidden in her office. He urged the senator to practice the speech in the adjacent [[Imperial Plaza|Senate Plaza]] so that he could continue searching the office for additional microphones. Mothma returned at sunrise, having learned from Rael that Semaj had been assisting the [[Axis network]] behind her back. Semaj admitted to helping Rael for the previous two years, claiming to have tried to protect Mothma. Angry and hurt at Semaj's betrayal, the senator told him that he had failed and immediately dismissed him from his position. Semaj stated that it had been an honor working for her and departed.<ref name="Welcome" />

Axis operative [[Kleya Marki]] contacted Semaj as he walked to the [[Imperial Senate Building|Senate Building]], and Semaj, struggling to control his emotions from the falling out, was unable to confirm whether or not Mothma was going ahead with her speech. Inside the Senate Building, Semaj encountered [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], who was preparing to extract Mothma after she spoke so that she could flee [[Coruscant]] for the [[Great Temple|rebel base]] on [[Yavin 4]]. He recognized Andor, and the two rushed together to a media lobby to wait for the senator's speech to begin. Aware that a previously planned extraction team under Senator [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] had been compromised by the [[Imperial Security Bureau]], Semaj watched a pair of unknown individuals with suspicion as they waited nearby. Mon Mothma denounced the [[Galactic Empire]]'s actions on Ghorman, mourning the death of truth and objective reality in the Imperial Senate and blaming [[Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] himself.<ref name="Welcome" />
[[File:Andor-EscapeFromTheSenate.png|thumb|250x250px|Beska attempts to arrest Mothma as they flee the senate building]]
After the speech, Andor brought Mothma into the lobby, where she was swarmed by [[journalist]]s. Semaj helped to clear the crowd away, but the ISB [[Beska|agent]] stopped the group, and, revealing her true identity, attempted to take Mothma into custody. Semaj shouted that the woman was a rebel [[spy]], distracting her long enough for Andor to shoot her and prevent the arrest. Armed with the agent's [[blaster]], Semaj urged Andor to escape with Mothma while he remained behind to handle the crowd. [[Stormtrooper]]s rushed in to capture Mothma soon after, but in the chaos, Semaj walked past them and escaped before the building could be fully locked down. The group reunited that evening at Rael's Coruscant [[Axis network safehouse|safehouse]]. When Semaj asked the senator if she was all right, she nodded and offered a smile of reborn trust. Semaj and Marki explained to Andor that the rebels intended to rewrite the story of Mothma’s escape, and that a Yavin escort would be utilized to relocate the senator to the rebel base after she gave another [[Declaration of the Rebel Alliance|speech]].<ref name="Welcome" />

===Birth of the Alliance===
{{Quote|Look, that probe, it was probably looking for us, specifically. We are carrying cargo highly valuable to the Rebellion, and desperately wanted by the Empire.|Erskin Semaj, to Hera Syndulla|<ref name="Secret Cargo" />}}
Mothma officially resigned from the [[Imperial Senate]], and Semaj and members of [[Gold Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Gold Squadron]] accompanied her into hiding<ref name="Secret Cargo" /> on her [[Taylander shuttle]] ''[[Chandrila Mistress]]''<ref name="Chandrila Mistress DB">{{Databank|chandrila-mistress|Chandrila Mistress}}</ref> and several [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber|Y-wing]] escorts. With Mon Mothma and her fellow rebels now fugitives, her friend Senator [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] arranged for the group to rendezvous with [[Phoenix Leader]] [[Hera Syndulla]] and her [[Spectres]] in deep space in order to [[Fuel|refuel]] their ships.<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

After Mothma's freighter docked with Hera's [[VCX-100 light freighter]] ''[[Ghost]]'', Semaj and [[Gold Leader]] [[Captain]] [[Jon Vander]] boarded the rebel ship. The two met Hera and her crew [[Garazeb Orrelios]], [[Ezra Bridger]], and the [[astromech droid]] [[C1-10P|Chopper]]. When Ezra asked what cargo they were carrying, Erskin told them they were not allowed aboard due to security conditions. Hera responded by telling them they were welcome aboard her ship. The ''Ghost'' then began refueling Mothma's freighter's Y-wing escorts.<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

While they were refueling, an argument broke out between the pilot [[Gold Two (rebellion)|Gold Two]] and the Spectres over secrecy and tactics. When Hera defended her crew, Semaj took a conciliatory stance and remarked that the [[X3-13|tactical infiltration pod]] that the Spectres had encountered earlier was probably looking for them. After an [[Arquitens-class command cruiser|''Arquitens''-class command cruiser]] and a [[Gozanti-class cruiser|''Gozanti''-class cruiser]] exited [[hyperspace]] and damaged Mothma's ship, Semaj, Mothma, and the remaining crew fled aboard the ''Ghost''. Together, with the Y-wing escorts, the rebels then fled to the [[Archeon Nebula]].<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

[[File:Secret_Cargo.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Semaj sits aboard the ''Ghost'' while Mon Mothma delivers her speech.]]
Following their escape, Semaj advised the former Senator Mothma to abandon their mission and return to a safe hiding place on [[Chandrila]]. Mothma disagreed and said that she would not hide because her presence at the meeting on [[Dantooine]] was not optional. Mothma then briefed the rebels about her plan to convene a meeting of the different rebel factions on Dantooine in order to form a [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]]. After escaping an Imperial [[Operation Handoff|trap]] in the Archeon Nebula, Semaj and his fellow rebels managed to reach Dantooine, where Mon Mothma delivered a speech to the assembled [[Rebel Alliance Navy|rebel fleet]].<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

===Road to war===
{{Quote|Commander Bridger, Senator Mothma has requested your presence.|Erskin Semaj, to Ezra Bridger|<ref name="The Occupation" />}}
After the Spectres arrived on Yavin 4 aboard the ''Ghost'', Erskin Semaj informed the Spectres that Mon Mothma had requested a meeting with them to discuss intelligence from the [[Lothal resistance group]] leader [[Ryder Azadi]] that the Empire was testing a [[TIE/D Defender Elite|new kind]] of [[TIE/d "Defender" Multi-Role Starfighter]]. The Spectres accepted the mission and infiltrated Lothal with the help of the [[crime lord]] [[Cikatro Vizago]].<ref name="The Occupation" /> Hera Syndulla managed to steal the prototype starfighter's [[flight data recorder]] and returned to Yavin 4 aboard Ryder's [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft|U-wing]]. Erskin and Mothma greeted Syndulla and were both pleased to see the flight recorder.<ref name="Kindred">{{Rebels|Kindred}}</ref>

Later, Erskin attended a high-level rebel briefing with Mon Mothma, Senator Organa, General Dodonna, and Syndulla to discuss the threat posed by the TIE/D Defender Elite to the Alliance's starfighters. After the Empire launched Protocol 13, Hera convinced Mon Mothma to authorize a [[Attack on Lothal|strike mission]] to take out the Imperial factories on Lothal.<ref name="Crawler Commandeers">{{Rebels|Crawler Commandeers}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Senator, let's forget this mission and get you back to Chandrila to a proper hiding place.''"<br/>"''No hiding, my presence at the meeting is not optional. Erskin, I trust them to get me there.|Erskin Semaj and Mon Mothma|<ref name="Secret Cargo" />}}
Erskin Semaj was a human male with brown eyes. A senatorial attaché, he wore a blue and white uniform patterned similarly to [[Special Forces Trackers Unit|Rebel SpecForce Pathfinders]] stationed on Yavin at the time.<ref name="Secret Cargo" /> Semaj was a loyal and protective servant of the rebel leader Mon Mothma. While he sometimes regarded her as too daring, he was a reliable aid and shared her beliefs in fighting for the galaxy's freedom.<ref name="DB" /> Semaj could also be brusque towards strangers. His pragmatism clashed with Mothma's idealism.<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

==Behind the scenes==
Erskin Semaj first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|Season Three]] episode "[[Secret Cargo]]," which first premiered on [[Disney XD]] on [[March 4]], [[2017]]. He was voiced by [[Josh Brener]].<ref name="Secret Cargo" /> He was first portrayed in live-action in "[[One Year Later]]," the first episode of the [[Disney+]] series [[Star Wars: Andor|''Andor's'']] [[Andor Season 2|second season]], which was released on [[April 22]], [[2025]]. He was portrayed by [[Pierro Niel-Mee]].<ref name="One Year Later" />

The character's name is a [[tuckerization]] of [[James Erskine]], Story Editor at Lucasfilm.

